<title>FRANCE: SGS-Thomson net earnings up, sees weaker Q1.</title>
<headline>SGS-Thomson net earnings up, sees weaker Q1.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net earnings				 625.5  vs	   526.5</p>
<p>    Net earnings per share ($)		4.50  vs	    4.03</p>
<p>    Operating				    799.4  vs	   651.0</p>
<p>    Pre-tax, pre minorities		  795.5  vs	   634.2</p>
<p>    Net revenues			     4,078.3  vs	 3,520.7</p>
<p>Q4</p>
<p>    Net earnings				 142.0  vs	   168.0</p>
<p>    Net earnings per share		    1.02  vs	    1.24</p>
<p>    Operating				    186.9  vs	   185.4</p>
<p>    Pre-tax, pre minorities		  181.0  vs	   183.3</p>
<p>    Net revenues			     1,058.9  vs	   974.7</p>
<p>NOTE - SGS-Thomson Microelectronics NV president and chief executive Pasquale Pistorio said in a statement that the first quarter 1997 revenues would be close to the third quarter 1996 levels. He added pricing pressure would continue and the gross margin could be slightly below fourth quarter 1996 levels.</p>
<p>He said that while first conditions continued to be uncertain he believed that the subsequent quarters in 1997 would show progressive improvement compared to the 1997 first quarter.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
